# ## 4. Results: the nine cases
#
# <a id="s4-1"></a>
#
# ### 4.1 The nine cases
#
# **Every ideal case gives F = 1 with every shot kept, and the protected cases keep {{ pct([c[3], c[6], c[9]] | map(attribute="acceptance") | min) }} to {{ pct([c[3], c[6], c[9]] | map(attribute="acceptance") | max) }} of their shots.** One noise profile, one base seed, {{ "{:,}".format(B.shots) }} shots per basis; each ± is one standard error.
#
# | Graph | Ideal | Noisy baseline | Protected: F after postselection, acceptance |
# |---|---|---|---|
# | 2016-inspired | {{ "%g"|format(c[1].fidelity) }} (case 1) | {{ F(c[2]) }} (case 2) | {{ F(c[3]) }}, {{ a3(c[3].acceptance) }} (case 3) |
# | Contemporary | {{ "%g"|format(c[4].fidelity) }} (case 4) | {{ F(c[5]) }} (case 5) | {{ F(c[6]) }}, {{ a3(c[6].acceptance) }} (case 6) |
# | Hyperbolic-inspired | {{ "%g"|format(c[7].fidelity) }} (case 7) | {{ F(c[8]) }} (case 8) | {{ F(c[9]) }}, {{ a3(c[9].acceptance) }} (case 9) |
#
# The table below gives every case the five measures the challenge asks every result to report, from the run records of the {{ REPORTED }} benchmark, the benchmark that fills the nine cases.

# %%
