# %% [markdown]
# <a id="s4-2"></a>
#
# ### 4.2 What protection buys, and what it costs
#
# **Most of the gain over the baseline comes from the transport, and the check adds to it only where it reads a spare path at the end of the circuit.** For each graph, the workbench sets the baseline, the move chain alone and the move chain with its XX check side by side: a table, then a bar per run of its F, and a second bar for a run's kept shots, with its acceptance. Their circuits are in section 3.5.
#
# | Graph | Baseline | Move chain | Move chain + XX check | The check's cost |
# |---|---|---|---|---|
# | 2016-inspired | {{ F(c[2]) }}, {{ c[2].two_qubit_gates }} gates | {{ F(mv.ibm2016) }}, {{ mv.ibm2016.two_qubit_gates }} gates | {{ F(c[3]) }} at {{ a3(c[3].acceptance) }}, {{ c[3].two_qubit_gates }} gates | a {{ "%.1f"|format(read_us) }} µs mid-circuit read; schedule {{ us(mv.ibm2016) }} → {{ us(c[3]) }} µs |
# | Contemporary | {{ F(c[5]) }}, {{ c[5].two_qubit_gates }} gates | {{ F(mv.contemporary) }}, {{ mv.contemporary.two_qubit_gates }} gates | {{ F(c[6]) }} at {{ a3(c[6].acceptance) }}, {{ c[6].two_qubit_gates }} gates | {{ c[6].two_qubit_gates - mv.contemporary.two_qubit_gates }} more gates, {{ c[6].qubits_used - mv.contemporary.qubits_used }} more qubits |
# | Hyperbolic-inspired | {{ F(c[8]) }}, {{ c[8].two_qubit_gates }} gates | {{ F(mv.hyperbolic) }}, {{ mv.hyperbolic.two_qubit_gates }} gates | {{ F(c[9]) }} at {{ a3(c[9].acceptance) }}, {{ c[9].two_qubit_gates }} gates | {{ c[9].two_qubit_gates - mv.hyperbolic.two_qubit_gates }} more gates, {{ c[9].qubits_used - mv.hyperbolic.qubits_used }} more qubits |

# %%
def side_by_side(processor):
    """The baseline, the move chain and the protected run on one graph, as the workbench compares them."""
    baseline, protected, *_ = CASES[processor]
    return wb.compare(*(wb.fetch(REPORTED, run) for run in (baseline, f"move-{processor}", protected)))

# %% [markdown]
# #### The 2016-inspired graph: the check does not pay
#
# **Its mid-circuit read holds the pair idle for {{ "%.1f"|format(read_us) }} µs, and F after postselection, {{ F(c[3]) }}, stays below the move chain alone, {{ F(mv.ibm2016) }}.** The graph has one path between its ports, so the check must reuse a qubit of the pair's path and read it mid-circuit first; appendix A.1 shows this holds even with no mid-circuit measurement error.{{ chk() }}

# %%
side_by_side("ibm2016")

# %% [markdown]
# #### The contemporary graph: the check pays
#
# **The check, on a spare path read at the end, adds {{ f4(c[6].fidelity - mv.contemporary.fidelity) }} to the move chain's F, more than twice the combined standard error, keeping {{ pct(c[6].acceptance) }} of shots.** The move chain alone already recovers most of the baseline's loss, from {{ c[5].two_qubit_gates }} two-qubit gates to {{ mv.contemporary.two_qubit_gates }}.{{ chk() }}

# %%
side_by_side("contemporary")

# %% [markdown]
# #### The hyperbolic-inspired graph: the check pays
#
# **The check adds {{ f4(c[9].fidelity - mv.hyperbolic.fidelity) }} to the move chain's F, more than twice the combined standard error, keeping {{ pct(c[9].acceptance) }} of shots, with {{ c[9].two_qubit_gates - mv.hyperbolic.two_qubit_gates }} more two-qubit gates and {{ c[9].qubits_used - mv.hyperbolic.qubits_used }} more qubits.**{{ chk() }}

# %%
side_by_side("hyperbolic")

